~ p1_wait_hint
Emily: Mom and Dad run like clockwork. [#thought]
Emily: If I sit by the living room clock, maybe the hours will slip by faster. [#thought]
=> END

~ p1_painting_fight
Leanne: Don't. Don't touch it. You don't get to touch her. [#leanne=fight_painting_leanne]
David: She was my daughter too, Lee.
Leanne: Then where were you? Every night it's the bills, the bank, the overtime—
David: Somebody had to keep the lights on in this house. [#david=fight_painting_david]
Leanne: She needed you here. Not the lights.
David: Don't put this on me. You know what you said to her that night.
=> END

~ p1_after
Emily: That night...? What did Mom say to me? [#thought]
Emily: The garage... I think I can get in now. [#thought]
=> END